#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# subdivide

#% text
# `subdivide(n)` gives the `n + 1` equally spaced values `[0, 1/n, 2/n, ..., 1]`.

#% text
# `subdivide(b, n)` gives `n + 1` equally spaced values from 0 to `b`; `subdivide(a, b, n)` from `a` to `b`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The values are `a + (b - a)*k/n` for `k = 0, 1, ..., n`: exact when the ends are exact, machine reals when an end is one.

#% item
# Both ends are included, so the list has `n + 1` elements; `n` must be a positive integer.

#% item
# Symbolic ends give symbolic values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
subdivide(4)
#% output
#= [0, 1/4, 1/2, 3/4, 1]

#% cell
subdivide(0, 10, 5)
#% output
#= [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Machine reals and symbolic ends:

#% cell
subdivide(1.0, 2, 4)
#% output
#= [1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 1.75, 2.0]

#% cell
subdivide(a, b, 2)
#% output
#= [a, a + (1/2)*(b - a), b]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Sample points for a table of values:

#% cell
map(x => [x, x^2], subdivide(0, 1, 4))
#% output
#= [[0, 0], [1/4, 1/16], [1/2, 1/4], [3/4, 9/16], [1, 1]]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The same values as a `range` with a fractional step:

#% cell
subdivide(0, 1, 4) == range(0, 1, 1/4)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `range`, `table`, `array`
